# Example env files — placeholders only

`.env.example` and `.env.demo.example` are committed checklists. They show **key names** and **shape**, not live values.

Real values belong only in gitignored `.env.local` / `.env.demo.local` (or Vercel). Never copy from those files into an example file.

## When adding or editing a key

1. Keep the existing file shape: `# ====` section banners, `# ---` subsections, `# name:` Console labels, and nearby key order.
2. Put the new key in the matching section. Do not dump keys at the bottom.
3. Use a descriptive snake_case placeholder, an empty value, or a truncated vendor prefix. Never a live secret or Appwrite `$id`.

```dotenv
# ✅ GOOD
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPWRITE_TICKETS_COLLECTION=tickets_collection_id
NEXT_APPWRITE_API_KEY=next_appwrite_api_key
ESIGN_TOKEN_SECRET=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
CRON_SECRET=cron_secret

# ❌ BAD — real IDs, tokens, or values copied from .env.local
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPWRITE_TICKETS_COLLECTION=69b8a201001f4e8c2a01
NEXT_APPWRITE_API_KEY=standard_...
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_51Abc...
CRON_SECRET=7f3a9c2e1b...
```

## Allowed non-secret defaults

These are OK because they are public, local, or flags — not credentials:

- Localhost URLs (`http://localhost:3000`)
- Public Appwrite endpoint (`https://fra.cloud.appwrite.io/v1`)
- Booleans / numbers (`true`, `false`, `30`, `90`)
- Documented public demo names (`caalm-demo`, `APP_MODE=demo`)
- Example domains already in the file (`caalmsolutions.com`)

## Never write

- Appwrite alphanumeric `$id` values (collection, bucket, project, database)
- API keys, tokens, private keys, webhook / cron / HMAC secrets
- Live Stripe keys (`sk_live_`, `pk_live_`)
- Anything read from `.env.local`, `.env.demo.local`, Vercel, or the Appwrite Console

Demo: add a key to `.env.demo.example` only if caalm-demo needs it, still as a placeholder.
